#! Navigation under utf32 (s133): the three astral-navigate files are NOT
#! copies — the same `bmp` sits at a different `character` in each. The
#! request on line 45 (`    let tail = "é中🐺👨‍👩é" != bmp`) is the
#! client->offset direction: the column is counted in this encoding's
#! units past astral, BMP, combining and ZWJ text. The references answer
#! from the declaration on line 21 (ASCII before it, so the same column
#! everywhere) is the byte->client direction: the use on line 45 must
#! come back at column 29 HERE and elsewhere in the other two. A rename
#! through the same position pins the edit range in this encoding too.
name      encoding/astral-navigate-utf32
profile   utf32-only
workspace fixtures

initialize
open      astral.lu
wait      diagnostics astral.lu
req       definition astral.lu 45:29
req       references astral.lu 21:8 decl
req       rename astral.lu 45:29 base
shutdown
